<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 14 March, from 1074 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/solomon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solomon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1074">1074 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">952 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Géza and Ladislaus defeat King Solomon of Hungary at Mogyoród</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dukes Géza and Ladislaus, claiming the throne, defeated their cousin King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> at Mogyoród and forced him to flee to the kingdom's western borderland. Géza was proclaimed king that year, but Solomon kept the western regions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geza-i-of-hungary">Géza I of Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-i-of-hungary">Ladislaus I of Hungary</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1309">1309 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">717 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A palace revolt in Granada deposes Muhammad III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Eid al-Fitr the citizens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> stormed palaces in the city, deposed the Nasrid emir Muhammad III and placed his brother Nasr on the throne. Muhammad's capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> had provoked an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, Aragon and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> against Granada.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-iii-of-granada">Muhammad III of Granada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1757">1757 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Admiral John Byng executed by firing squad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Convicted of failing to do his utmost to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Minorca</a>, Byng was shot on the deck of HMS Monarch at Portsmouth. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voltaire">Voltaire</a> mocked the English for killing an admiral 'to encourage the others'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1794">1794 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Eli Whitney patents the cotton gin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Whitney's machine separated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> fibre from seeds far faster than by hand. It made short-staple cotton highly profitable and fuelled a vast expansion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1879">1879 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Einstein is born in Ulm</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Einstein's theories of special and general relativity transformed ideas of space, time and gravity. He won the 1921 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> for explaining the photoelectric effect.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1900">1900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gold Standard Act puts the dollar on gold</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President McKinley signed the act fixing the dollar's value in gold and ending the long political fight over free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>. The US left the gold standard domestically in 1933.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Penicillin saves its first American patient</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anne Miller, dying of streptococcal blood poisoning after a miscarriage, was treated at a New Haven hospital with a scarce supply of penicillin. She recovered and lived to the age of 90.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jack Ruby convicted of murdering Lee Harvey Oswald</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Dallas jury found the nightclub owner guilty of shooting Kennedy's accused assassin on live television and sentenced him to death. The verdict was overturned, and Ruby died before a retrial.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 14 March <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-nunez-de-caceres"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-nunez-de-caceres.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Núñez de Cáceres</span><span class="tp">1772–1846</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-emmanuel-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Emmanuel II</span><span class="tp">1820–1878</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/umberto-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/umberto-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Umberto I</span><span class="tp">1844–1900</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-einstein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-einstein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Einstein</span><span class="tp">1879–1955</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-ii-prince-of-monaco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-ii-prince-of-monaco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert II, Prince of Monaco</span><span class="tp">b. 1958</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 14 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-ringelheim"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/matilda-of-ringelheim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Matilda of Ringelheim</span><span class="tp">c. 892–968</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-henry-prince-of-orange"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-henry-prince-of-orange.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick Henry, Prince of Orange</span><span class="tp">1584–1647</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juan-manuel-de-rosas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juan Manuel de Rosas</span><span class="tp">1793–1877</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/klement-gottwald"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/klement-gottwald.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Klement Gottwald</span><span class="tp">1896–1953</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-hatta"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mohammad-hatta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mohammad Hatta</span><span class="tp">1902–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lennart-meri"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lennart-meri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lennart Meri</span><span class="tp">1929–2006</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
